[Oracle -> Postgre] App-DB Dependency Code Changes & Progress Tracking [Java-Oracle]




Description

Background
After Oracle → PostgreSQL DB schema conversion completes (Job 2), the Java application code requires targeted changes to remain compatible with the transformed PostgreSQL database. These changes are driven by the 31 Oracle-Java dependency rules applied and the ones detected during assessment and stored in Db-dependency/Java-Oracle-dependency.json. This job (Job 3) reads those findings, applies remediations from the Oracle-Java Remediation, and produces a modified Java codebase with a post-transformation report and a separate GitHub commit.

For M-Basic and M-Container-Mono pathways, additional configuration file and infrastructure-level changes are required beyond violation remediations to ensure the containerized/cloud-ready application connects correctly to the transformed PostgreSQL database.

