FR4: Code Transformation — All Pathways (Common)

On confirmation, the system SHALL execute the following against the Java source codebase:

Read Java-Oracle-dependency.json findings

For each finding where the corresponding rule is selected:

Look up remediation in Oracle-Java Remediation KB JSON (placeholder: <oracle-java-remediation-kb>.json)

Apply remediation to the affected Java source file(s)

Track change: file modified, rule applied, line(s) changed, remediation ID

Generate change tracking metadata for use in Post-Transformation Report

FR5: Additional Changes — M-Basic Pathway

For M-Basic (cloud readiness) pathway, in addition to violation remediations, the system SHALL apply the following PostgreSQL compatibility changes:

Datasource Configuration:

Update application.properties / application.yml:

spring.datasource.url → PostgreSQL JDBC URL format (jdbc:postgresql://[host]:[port]/[dbname])

spring.datasource.driver-class-name → org.postgresql.Driver

spring.datasource.username / spring.datasource.password → placeholder values with inline comment

Replace Oracle JDBC driver dependency in pom.xml / build.gradle:

Remove: ojdbc dependency

Add: postgresql JDBC driver dependency (latest stable version)

ORM / Persistence Configuration (if applicable):

Update hibernate.dialect → org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect

Update persistence.xml or JPA configuration if present

Flag Oracle-specific JPA annotations or named queries for manual review

Cloud Datasource Compatibility:

If cloud-managed DB service endpoint pattern detected:

AWS RDS: add ?ssl=true&sslmode=require

Azure PostgreSQL: add ?sslmode=require&sslfactory=org.postgresql.ssl.NonValidatingFactory

GCP Cloud SQL: add ?socketFactory=com.google.cloud.sql.postgres.SocketFactory

Flag for manual review: "Verify cloud DB endpoint and credentials before deployment"

Connection Pool:

If Oracle UCP detected: replace with HikariCP configuration

Add HikariCP dependency to pom.xml / build.gradle if not present

FR6: Additional Changes — M-Container-Mono Pathway

For M-Container-Mono (containerization) pathway, in addition to violation remediations and all M-Basic datasource changes (FR7), the system SHALL apply the following container-level PostgreSQL compatibility changes:

Dockerfile:

Replace Oracle JDBC driver COPY / ADD instructions

Add PostgreSQL DB connection environment variable declarations with placeholders:



  ENV DB_HOST=<placeholder>
  ENV DB_PORT=5432
  ENV DB_NAME=<placeholder>
  ENV DB_USER=<placeholder>
  ENV DB_PASSWORD=<placeholder>
Add inline comments flagging placeholder values for manual replacement

docker-compose.yml (if present):

Update DB service environment variables to PostgreSQL format

Replace Oracle DB service definition with PostgreSQL service:

yaml



  db:
    image: postgres:15
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: <placeholder>
      POSTGRES_USER: <placeholder>
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: <placeholder>
    ports:
      - "5432:5432"
Kubernetes Manifests (if present):

Update DB environment variable references to PostgreSQL format using Secret references:

yaml



  env:
    - name: DB_URL
      valueFrom:
        secretKeyRef:
          name: db-secret
          key: url
Generate sample db-secret.yaml Secret manifest with placeholder PostgreSQL values

Flag for manual review: "Apply db-secret.yaml with actual PostgreSQL credentials before deployment"

Health Check Configuration:

If Oracle-specific health check SQL detected (e.g., SELECT 1 FROM DUAL):

Replace with: SELECT 1

Flag for manual review

CI-CD Pipeline Files (if detected):

No automated changes applied

Flag Oracle JDBC driver references for manual review

Add inline comment where possible

Phase 3: Artifacts
FR7: Post-Transformation Report
Covered in Feature 5. Job 3 triggers report generation on transformation completion.

FR8: GitHub Commit
Covered in Feature 6. Job 3 triggers a separate GitHub commit to target branch on transformation completion.

FR9: Artifacts Phase Completion
Once Post-Transformation Report and GitHub Commit are both complete, Job 3 status updates to "Completed" in left panel. Job 4 (Validation / Test Artifacts) CTA becomes available.

